clueweb09-en0007-58-02068.150 Save thousands of dollars by building your own fence. Email Send to Phone Print Article Add to Favorites Flag Article [Share] Instructions Difficulty: Moderate Things You’ll Need: Saw Hammer Screws or nails hole digger concrete mix Treated lumber Step1 You first need to lay out your fence. This will give you a great idea of how many posts and fencing material you will need. Step2 It is recommended that each post is concreted in the ground. Fill the concrete around the fence post to ground level to prevent rotting. I would dig the hole 2 1/2 - 3 feet deep
clueweb09-en0007-58-02068.225 ground. Fill the concrete around the fence post to ground level to prevent rotting. I would dig the hole 2 1/2 - 3 feet deep to avoid frost heaving. If you are looking for a 6 foot fence, I would purchase 10' 4x4 treated lumber. Step3 Once the hole is dug (I would use a 6 inch auger) Place your post in the ground. Fill it with concrete. Now check the level and plumb of the post. It should be level on all four sides. With a good thick concrete, you should be able to move the post easily, yet
